## ⇁  Install plugin manager

To install the plugin manager run the code below
MACRO_CODE
PGNDIR="$HOME/.local/lib/tec/pgn"
git clone https://github.com/roachme/tec-nine.git "$PGNDIR/nine"
MACRO_CODE
Note: \
1. Make sure the repo dirname has NO prefix MACRO_INLINE_CODE tec- MACRO_INLINE_CODE. The same goes for any plugin you install \
2. MACRO_INLINE_CODE "$PGNDIR" MACRO_INLINE_CODE is the path set in MACRO_INLINE_CODE tec.cfg MACRO_INLINE_CODE.
   Make sure MACRO_INLINE_CODE PGNDIR MACRO_INLINE_CODE is the same as MACRO_INLINE_CODE base.pgn MACRO_INLINE_CODE in MACRO_INLINE_CODE tec.cfg MACRO_INLINE_CODE shown above.


## ⇁  Basic workflow
1. To initialize the util type in MACRO_INLINE_CODE tec init MACRO_INLINE_CODE
2. Now you're ready to create an environment: MACRO_INLINE_CODE tec env add test MACRO_INLINE_CODE
3. Once the task environment is created you can fill it with tasks: MACRO_INLINE_CODE tec add test1 MACRO_INLINE_CODE
4. Add one more task: MACRO_INLINE_CODE tec add test2 MACRO_INLINE_CODE
5. List all your tasks in the current environment: MACRO_INLINE_CODE tec ls MACRO_INLINE_CODE
6. Show the content of a task: MACRO_INLINE_CODE tec cat test1 MACRO_INLINE_CODE
7. Sync with the current task: MACRO_INLINE_CODE tec cd MACRO_INLINE_CODE
8. Or quickly switch to the previous task: MACRO_INLINE_CODE tec cd - MACRO_INLINE_CODE


## ⇁  Tips
1. Use MACRO_INLINE_CODE tec help MACRO_INLINE_CODE to get a list of commands.
2. Or MACRO_INLINE_CODE tec help COMMAND MACRO_INLINE_CODE to get help on a specified command.
